# TYFZA1 native FTTR service policies, loaded at controller startup.
# One service per ONU. Exact serial matches take precedence over '*'.
# No active rows means inventory only. Select network policy explicitly.
#
# serial: 16 hexadecimal digits in vendor-first wire order, or *
# kind: 0=Ethernet, 2=VEIP; ordinal: zero-based within that actual MIB class
# kind shared: attach all reported Ethernet and VEIP UNIs; ordinal must be 0
# shared-mcast/shared-ctc also install the original remote multicast recipe.
# Local fttr-mc admission is not enabled yet; these kinds provision OMCI only
# for multicast, while the unicast bridge path works as for shared.
# These explicit policies do not import the full factory default configuration.
# slot: ASIC9690/FPGA2 1..7, FPGA1 1
# priority: 0..7; VID: 0..4094, or none for transparent mode
# fixed/assured/maximum: hardware grant units, as in fttrctl service
# bridge: existing, up Linux bridge, or - for OMCI provisioning only
# The controller creates fttr-u<ID> with outer 802.1Q VID=GEM Port-ID.
#
# serial            kind ordinal slot priority VID  fixed assured maximum bridge
